<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 8: </span>Mean and standard deviation of the correlation to functional correctness of different variations of <span id="A1.T8.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">MATCH</span> (<math id="A1.T8.m79" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>τ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau</annotation></semantics></math> = Kendall, <math id="A1.T8.m80" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{s}</annotation></semantics></math> = Spearman, and <math id="A1.T8.m81" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{p}</annotation></semantics></math> = Pearson) across programming languages from HumanEval and correlation to human preferences on CoNaLa Datasets. Correlations are presented in <a href="#S7.T4" title="In 7 Analysis ‣ MATCH: Task-Driven Code Evaluation through Contrastive Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Table</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>.</figcaption>
</figure>
