<span id="A2.tab3.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top">
<span id="A2.tab3.1.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.tab3.1.1.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Example 3: MATCH has a better understanding of the code semantics.</span></span>
</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A2.tab3.1.2" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A2.tab3.1.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_b ltx_border_l ltx_border_r" style="padding-top:1pt;padding-bottom:1pt;">
<span id="A2.tab3.1.2.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top">
<span id="A2.tab3.1.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_p">Both code candidates fail to correctly implement the task. The first candidate is incorrect, while the second candidate sums the binary digits instead of the decimal digits. The MATCH score accurately reflects the errors in both candidates, unlike the ICE-Score, which misclassifies the second candidate as correct.</span>
</span></td></tr>
</tbody>
</table></div><div class="ltx_flex_break"></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_1">
