<span id="A2.tab4.1.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.tab4.1.1.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Example 4: MATCH Effectively Differentiating between correct and incorrect code</span></span>
</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A2.tab4.1.2" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A2.tab4.1.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_b ltx_border_l ltx_border_r" style="padding-top:1pt;padding-bottom:1pt;">
<span id="A2.tab4.1.2.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top">
<span id="A2.tab4.1.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_p">The first code candidate correctly downloads a file, while the second incorrectly attempts to open a file without downloading it. The MATCH score reflects this, but the CodeBERTScore does not adequately differentiate between the candidates, and the ICE-Score gives both a score of 0.</span>
